  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Developing a human-big cats conflict mitigation model for the benefit of the local communities and at the same time survival of big cats in Assam, India, Phase-II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to build positive attitudes towards big cat conservation with emphasis on tiger conservation and to reduce the conflict by minimizing loss of big cats and human lives. The project will, (1) Develop awareness programs and involve people and local administration in mitigating conflict; (2) Maintain support for Rapid Response Teams with capture and transport equipment; (3) Maintain local response teams to respond to tiger and leopard encounters; and (4) Continue training Forest Department staff and local administrators and members of the Rapid Response Teams and Primary Response Teams. Rapid Response Teams (RRT) and Primary Response Teams (PRT) formed with grant support will tackle human-tiger and human-leopard conflict situations. The grant will contribute to the salaries of the 15 trained forest staff, 3 veterinarians, support necessary training, and purchase of essential supplies.</narrative>
  </description>
